WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.020
In the sixteen hundreds, a man planted a willow stem in a pot of dried soil.

2
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.080
The stem weighed five pounds.

3
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:12.460
The soil weighed two hundred pounds.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.540
Five years later, he reported a tree of about one hundred sixty nine pounds.

5
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.520
The soil was only about two ounces lighter.

6
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.100
So where does a plant's mass come from?

7
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.920
And how does sunlight end up stored in sugar?

8
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.060
The answer starts with photosynthesis.

9
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.780
Plants, algae and cyanobacteria use light energy to turn carbon dioxide and water

10
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.340
into sugar. They release oxygen.

11
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.160
The sugar is glucose, a small sugar molecule with six carbon atoms.

12
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:49.900
With formulas: six carbon dioxide plus six water plus light energy makes one glucose

13
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.500
plus six oxygen molecules.

14
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.980
Count the atoms. On the left, there are six carbon, twelve hydrogen and eighteen

15
00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.620
oxygen atoms. On the right, there are exactly the same.

16
00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.040
This is conservation of matter.

17
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.140
In a chemical change, atoms are rearranged, never created or destroyed.

18
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:11.563
Now the willow makes sense.

19
00:01:12.323 --> 00:01:17.143
The carbon and much of the oxygen in its sugar came from carbon dioxide in the air.

20
00:01:17.943 --> 00:01:19.463
The hydrogen came from water.

21
00:01:20.323 --> 00:01:24.303
The soil gave water and a small amount of minerals, so the dried soil barely

22
00:01:24.303 --> 00:01:28.543
changed. He weighed the tree alive, so part of its gain was water.

23
00:01:29.443 --> 00:01:34.363
Most of a plant's dry mass, the mass left after drying, is built from carbon taken

24
00:01:34.363 --> 00:01:35.823
in as carbon dioxide.

25
00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:42.417
In plants and algae, photosynthesis happens in the chloroplast, a green organelle in

26
00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:46.497
leaf cells. Inside it, stacks of membranes hold chlorophyll.

27
00:01:47.337 --> 00:01:51.017
Chlorophyll is a green pigment that absorbs light, mostly red and blue.

28
00:01:51.857 --> 00:01:56.157
That captured energy powers the reactions that split water and build glucose.

29
00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.477
The oxygen released comes from the split water.

30
00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.130
Energy is conserved too.

31
00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.110
Light energy is not used up or made.

32
00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:10.930
It is transformed into chemical energy, energy held in the arrangement of atoms in

33
00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:16.670
molecules. Glucose and oxygen together hold more chemical energy than the carbon

34
00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:18.930
dioxide and water they came from.

35
00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:24.750
So a plant's dry mass comes mostly from carbon dioxide in the air, and sunlight is

36
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.650
stored as chemical energy in sugar.
